# SideRun env template — copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
# Expo only exposes variables with the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix to the client bundle.

# ── Backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No database or server is required. Auth + data + (simulated) realtime run
# fully on-device via services/localClient.js (AsyncStorage-backed). The old
# Supabase / MemFire variables below are NO LONGER USED by the app and are kept
# only as a reference in case a real cloud backend is reintroduced later.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.memfiredb.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-anon-key

# ── Optional third-party APIs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenWeatherMap (see WeatherScreen.js / HomeScreen.js). Optional — when unset,
# the app falls back to built-in mock weather, so demos still work offline.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=
